            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Failover.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "I feel the defined enum may not be very helpful.\n\nFor instance, if the BMC is managed by multiple Redfish clients, we won\u2019t be able to identify which client initiated the Failover request \u2014 and the same limitation applies to SystemConfig.\n\nUsing free-form text, on the other hand, allows us to include requester-specific client information.\n\nBut I don't have strong preference though."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Failover.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I can see what you're saying, we just don't need that level of granularity yet.  If we do end up needing that, then we could add a new free format property."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Failover.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "This one jumped out at me a little as putting external interface protocol specifics in PDI could be a bit of a problem later (like what if IPMI or SPDM were to support a fail over? Would we add a new IPMI or would a generic \"ExternalClient\" be better)? We can always fix later so wont prevent a +1 from me."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/Failover.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I think we'd want to distinguish between IPMI & Redfish.  But can revisit in future if necessary."
                }
            ],
